Ok, I've been experiencing a few probs with NH 3.0........ I got down to dungeon level 30 or so I believe, and found the CASTLE level. (I could tell it was because I had a blindfold and had eaten a floating eye)... I saved the game right there... And then.. POOF... Whenever I restore it it locks up.. I have 612K free and am running one that wasn't compiled with Polymorph Self or spells.. It might be a memory problem, but I really don't think so.... 
 
Anyways.. I don't disagree with the thing about spells being slowly(actually, fastly) taken from your memory when you cast them... I think it should be like on Nethack 1.0 (or 2.0??) where spells last forever.. But I think the 'genocide' spell should be taken out.. It seems that is too powerful. Unless it only has like a .1% chance of working..
 
PLUS, Why would anyone want a bag??? If you put items in a bag its like your still carrying the same amount of weight.. I think if you put items in a bag, it should reduce the items weight by AT LEAST 1/2... I think it is much easier hauling a bag around on your shoulder then carrying each item seperately(sp..)... 
 
Hum. I guess i'll include a few spoilers.. (They don't actually spoil the game. hehe)

Ok.. To kill a medusa you need a blindfold, a mirror, And if you have eaten a floating eye it will make it MUCH, MUCH easier.. Wear the blindfold, find the medusa, and apply the mirror to it.
 
Shops -=- Ok.. Get a PICK-AXE and dig at the shops walls.. At first it will say the walls are too hard to dig into.. Keep trying. After about 10-15 trys you will make a hole in the wall, in which you can plunder the shop.
 
Dragons -=- Find a REFLECTIVE shield, it will REFLECT there breath and may cause damage to other monsters in the area. 
 
Armor -=- Try to find some boots of speed, as far as I can see those are probably THE BEST armor around.. If you get that from a shop on level 2, GREAT.. Walk back, hit a monster, Walk back, hit a monster.. That usually works 'till about level 10 when the monsters get faster.... DO NOT attack the Shopkeeper.. hehe.. I have found them hard even on EXP level 12...
 
